# PLAN — @hiprax/use-seo hardening pass

This plan fixes **7 genuine, adversarially-verified issues** found by a whole-system,
non-linear review of `@hiprax/use-seo` (v0.3.2). Every finding below was confirmed by two
independent reviewers tracing the real code paths (0 rejected). The codebase is otherwise
in excellent shape — this plan touches only what is demonstrably wrong or a clear
best-practice gap, ships dedicated tests for each change, and keeps everything backward
compatible per project policy.

Baseline at plan time: `npm run build` ✅, `npm test` ✅ (512 tests), `npm run typecheck` ✅,
`npm run lint` ✅. `npm run format:check` ❌ **locally on Windows** (CRLF drift — Finding 7).
All committed blobs are LF, so CI (Linux) is green; the local failure is fixed in Phase 1.

---

## Section 1 — MANDATORY EXECUTION PROTOCOL (read before every phase)

Follow this protocol verbatim for **every task in every phase**:

- **Back up before modifying (non-negotiable).** Before the first non-read-only operation on
  an **existing** file, copy it to `<path>.tmp` (e.g. `src/useSEO.ts` → `src/useSEO.ts.tmp`).
  Brand-new files need no backup. If a change proves wrong or a judge rejects it, restore from
  the `.tmp` copy. After the task is validated, delete every `.tmp` you created. **Zero `.tmp`
  files may remain**, and none may ever be staged/committed. Confirm they are gone before
  declaring a task complete.
- **Never stop to ask the operator or wait for confirmation.** There is no human available. If
  anything is ambiguous, has multiple viable approaches, or looks wrong, summon **two new
  independent judge agents (two `claude-sonnet-5`, max effort, read-only/sandboxed — no Edit/
  Write/NotebookEdit)** to analyze it independently and return verdicts; act on the
  best-reasoned verdict. Zero questions to the user.
- **Read the referenced files before making any change.** Analyze **non-linearly**: trace each
  definition to all call sites and each usage back to its definition; judge correctness from
  the whole-system view.
- **Do not blindly trust this plan.** Re-verify each step yourself first. If a step looks
  wrong, summon two new independent judge agents (two `claude-sonnet-5`, max effort,
  sandboxed) for a final verdict with reasoning before proceeding.
- **Add tests** for the task (mirror the existing `tests/` structure and style).
- **After implementing, run the relevant build/compile/test command** to verify the change.
- **Always keep independent judges watching.** For every task, and for every agent you spawn,
  summon **two new independent judge agents (two `claude-sonnet-5`, max effort, sandboxed)** to
  validate the work in progress. Before marking any task complete, launch two fresh sandboxed
  judges to validate the work and progress; only when both confirm do you proceed.
- **Update the Task Summary Checklist** (tick each box you complete).
- **Fix ANY issue, error, or warning you encounter** — even pre-existing, even not caused by
  you. Do not check whether a problem is pre-existing; do not use git history/reverts to
  sidestep it; just fix it. All tests must end **100% green, no errors, no warnings**.
- **Work strictly in order; skip nothing; never pause between tasks.** Install packages,
  create files, and modify files as needed (read existing files before editing them).
- **ULTRATHINK.**

After all tasks in a phase are done, run `npm run build` (and `npm test`) to confirm
everything compiles and passes; fix any errors before finishing the phase.

> Integration (git add/commit/push/tag/release) is handled **outside** this plan. No phase
> performs any git or release operation. Version/CHANGELOG bookkeeping is plain file edits
> only (Phase 8), never `npm version` (which would create a git tag).

