## Verified findings (what we are fixing)

| # | Severity | File | Summary |
|---|----------|------|---------|
| 1 | high→med | `src/useSEO.ts:511` | `clearSEOTags()` never resets `prevConfigRef`/`jsonLdScriptsRef`; re-rendering with unchanged props after a clear never re-applies tags — head stays empty. |
| 2 | medium | `src/useSEO.ts:709` | `article:published_time`/`modified_time`/`expiration_time` linger after their props are removed (no cleanup else-branch), unlike the sibling `article:section`. |
| 3 | low | `src/utils/validation.ts:250` | `inferImageMimeType` matches a dotted extension inside a **query string** of an extensionless URL → bogus `og:image:type`. |
| 4 | medium | `src/utils/robots.ts:80` | Serializer emits Google-invalid `max-snippet:none` / `max-video-preview:none` (only `max-image-preview` accepts `none`; the others take an integer — `0` means "none"). |
| 5 | med→low | `src/useSEO.ts:287` | Two live `useSEO` instances writing the same single-value tag: instance B tracks (and `clearSEOTags`-removes) an element instance A created (marker-based tracking can't tell ownership). |
| 6 | low | `src/useSEO.ts:1104` | `twitter:player` (and `twitter:player:stream`) emitted for `http:` URLs though the type is documented "HTTPS-only" — no warning. |
| 7 | medium | `.prettierrc` + repo root | No `.gitattributes`/`.editorconfig`; with `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows the working tree becomes CRLF and `format:check`/`verify`/`prepublishOnly` fail locally. |

