## Phase 1 — Line-ending normalization infra (Finding 7)

**Why:** `.prettierrc` pins `endOfLine: lf` but nothing enforces LF in git. On Windows with
`core.autocrlf=true`, `src/types.ts`, `src/useSEO.ts`, and `tests/useSEO.test.tsx` check out
as CRLF and fail `prettier --check`, breaking `npm run format:check`, `npm run verify`, and
`prepublishOnly` for any Windows contributor. All committed blobs are already LF
(`git ls-files --eol` → `i/lf` for all), so normalization rewrites **no** blobs. This phase
runs first so every later phase edits LF files on a clean base.

**Tasks:**
1. **Create `.gitattributes`** at repo root:
   ```gitattributes
   # Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and working tree.
   * text=auto eol=lf

   # Explicit LF for the source/tooling file types (belt-and-suspenders).
   *.ts   text eol=lf
   *.tsx  text eol=lf
   *.js   text eol=lf
   *.cjs  text eol=lf
   *.mjs  text eol=lf
   *.json text eol=lf
   *.md   text eol=lf
   *.yml  text eol=lf
   *.yaml text eol=lf

   # Never touch binary blobs.
   *.png  binary
   *.jpg  binary
   *.ico  binary
   ```
2. **Create `.editorconfig`** at repo root (editor-level consistency, matches `.prettierrc`):
   ```editorconfig
   root = true

   [*]
   charset = utf-8
   end_of_line = lf
   insert_final_newline = true
   trim_trailing_whitespace = true
   indent_style = space
   indent_size = 2

   [*.md]
   trim_trailing_whitespace = false
   ```
3. **Renormalize + verify.** Run `git add --renormalize .` (content no-op — all blobs already
   LF), then normalize the working-tree files: `npx prettier --write "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
   "tests/**/*.{ts,tsx}"` (or re-checkout) so the three CRLF files become LF on disk. Confirm:
   `npm run format:check` ✅, `npm run lint` ✅, `npm run typecheck` ✅, `npm test` ✅.
   Confirm `.npmignore` already excludes `.gitattributes` and `.editorconfig` (it does —
   verify; the published tarball is unaffected because `files` is `["dist","README.md","LICENSE"]`).
   Add a `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` note under a new **Tooling** subsection.

**No `src/` behavior change.** Purely tooling + working-tree normalization.

