## Phase 2 — `clearSEOTags()` state reset (Finding 1)

**Why:** `clearSEOTags` (`src/useSEO.ts:511-522`) removes the DOM elements and clears
`addedElements.current`, but leaves `prevConfigRef.current` and `jsonLdScriptsRef.current`
stale. The main effect bails at `src/useSEO.ts:632-635` when `configJSON ===
prevConfigRef.current`. So after `clearSEOTags()`, a re-render with an identically-serializing
config skips the effect and the just-deleted tags are never recreated — the head stays empty
until a prop actually changes. The unmount-cleanup effect already resets
`jsonLdScriptsRef.current.clear()` at `src/useSEO.ts:1571`, confirming the reset is intended
on teardown; it is simply missing from `clearSEOTags`.

**Tasks:**
1. In `clearSEOTags` (`src/useSEO.ts:511-522`), after `addedElements.current.clear()`, add:
   ```ts
   // Invalidate change-detection + JSON-LD reconciliation state so the next
   // effect run re-applies every tag from scratch. Without this, a re-render
   // with an unchanged config would hit the early-return in the main effect
   // and never recreate the tags we just removed. Mirrors the unmount-cleanup
   // effect below.
   prevConfigRef.current = '';
   jsonLdScriptsRef.current.clear();
   ```
   (`prevConfigRef` is the load-bearing reset; `jsonLdScriptsRef.clear()` mirrors the unmount
   effect and keeps the two teardown paths symmetric.)
2. **Tests** in `tests/useSEO.test.tsx` (Hook Return Methods): render with
   `{ title, description, structuredData }`; assert tags present; `act(clearSEOTags())`; assert
   removed; **rerender with the identical props (a fresh object with the same values)** and
   assert `meta[name="description"]`, an OG tag, and the `script[type="application/ld+json"]`
   are all restored. Add a same-reference variant too.
3. Update the `clearSEOTags` JSDoc to note it resets change-detection state so a subsequent
   render re-applies tags. Add a `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` **Fixed** entry (file paths).

