## Phase 3 — Article-date cleanup consistency (Finding 2)

**Why:** `article:published_time`/`article:modified_time`/`article:expiration_time`
(`src/useSEO.ts:709-723`) are emitted with bare `if` blocks and **no** cleanup, while the
sibling single-value tag `article:section` (`src/useSEO.ts:1031-1039`) has an
`else { removeMarkedElements('meta[property="article:section"]', addedElements.current); }`.
All three date props are in the change snapshot (`:576-578`) and deps array (`:1470-1472`), so
the effect re-runs when they drop — the tags just never get torn down. An SPA nav from an
article to a non-article page (same hook instance) leaves stale `article:*` dates in the DOM
for crawlers/scrapers. The cleanup-policy comment (`:1441-1460`) lists `article:section` as
cleaned-up but never places the dates in either bucket → oversight, not intent.

**Tasks:**
1. In `src/useSEO.ts`, give each of the three date branches an `else` mirroring
   `article:section`:
   ```ts
   if (publishedTime) {
     updateMetaInternal({ property: 'article:published_time' }, publishedTime);
   } else {
     removeMarkedElements('meta[property="article:published_time"]', addedElements.current);
   }
   if (modifiedTime) {
     updateMetaInternal({ property: 'article:modified_time' }, modifiedTime);
   } else {
     removeMarkedElements('meta[property="article:modified_time"]', addedElements.current);
   }
   if (expirationTime) {
     updateMetaInternal({ property: 'article:expiration_time' }, expirationTime);
   } else {
     removeMarkedElements('meta[property="article:expiration_time"]', addedElements.current);
   }
   ```
   Only hook-created (`data-use-seo="true"`) elements are removed; user-authored ones are
   preserved.
2. **Tests** (Article Dates block): for each of the three tags, render with the date set (via
   `renderHook` rerender), assert present, rerender with the prop unset, assert the marked
   meta is removed — mirroring the existing `article:section` cleanup test. Also assert a
   user-authored `article:published_time` (no marker) survives.
3. Update the cleanup-policy comment (`src/useSEO.ts:1441-1460`) to list the article dates
   among the cleaned-up single-value tags. Update the README "Article Extensions"/"Article
   Metadata" cleanup note. Add a `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` **Fixed** entry.

