## Phase 4 — `inferImageMimeType` query-string fix (Finding 3)

**Why:** The regex `/\.([a-z0-9]+)(?:[?#].*)?$/i` (`src/utils/validation.ts:250`) makes the
query/hash group optional, so with the `$` anchor it backtracks to the last `.ext` **anywhere**
before end-of-string — including inside a query string. `inferImageMimeType(
'https://img.example.com/render?w=100&file=photo.png')` returns `'image/png'` for an
extensionless path. Called at `src/useSEO.ts:836` and `:866` to fill `og:image:type`, so a
user passing such a URL with no explicit `type` gets a fabricated `<meta property=
"og:image:type" content="image/png">`.

**Tasks:**
1. In `src/utils/validation.ts`, strip the query/hash **before** extracting the extension so
   only the path is considered:
   ```ts
   // Consider only the path segment — strip any query/hash first so an
   // extension embedded in a query value (e.g. `/render?file=photo.png`) on an
   // extensionless path is NOT mistaken for the resource extension.
   const path = url.split(/[?#]/, 1)[0] ?? url;
   const pathMatch = path.match(/\.([a-z0-9]+)$/i);
   if (!pathMatch?.[1]) {
     return undefined;
   }
   ```
   (Keep the rest of the function unchanged. `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is on, hence the
   `?? url` guard on the split result.)
2. **Tests** in `tests/utils/validation.test.ts` (inferImageMimeType): assert
   `'.../render?w=100&file=photo.png'` → `undefined`; `'.../dynamic-image?ratio=1.5'` →
   `undefined`; and confirm the existing path-extension-with-query cases (e.g.
   `'https://example.com/image.png?v=2'`, `'.../image.jpg#frag'`) still resolve correctly.
3. Add a `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` **Fixed** entry (file paths).

